A||||9||GT Bastard||Pulling the top end... any suggestions/tips?||||11||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||05-13-2000||04:41 PM||||Well, I'm finally fed-up with my exhaust leak, and puff of smoke and startup.  One of my exhaust manifold bolts in the rear is broken off from previous owner, but both are leaking.  What I plan on doing is pulling the heads off completely and having my father port them while they're out.  Then he's going to freshen up the valves, new seals, new springs, etc. I've been studying my chiltons manual day and night!  It's going to be a mess for awhile, but I think it will be fairly easy as long as I keep track of what goes where.  I plan on having my existing manifolds ported and welded before reinstalling them.  Any advice on what to watch out for when I start pulling her apart?  ||||reg||11
Z||000001||Phil||05-13-2000||06:31 PM||||Soak them well with penetrating oil-snapped bolts are lots of fun.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||05-13-2000||06:38 PM||||I've already started.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||05-13-2000||07:34 PM||||I still mark all the wires and vacuum hoses with masking tape and write where they go. Saves lots of time later on. Buy a box of heavy duty zip-loc baggies to put bolts, nuts, washers, and other small parts in, then label the bags. The main problem is the limited, tight space within the Fiero engine compartment, but you'll manage ok.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||05-13-2000||08:59 PM||||Do you think I should have my injectors cleaned while everything is out?  There's a guy here in town that supposedly does this pretty reasonably.||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||05-13-2000||10:42 PM||||I have no idea what condition your injectors are in or if they need cleaning, but now is certainly the time to do all that kind of stuff while it's all apart.||||reg||1
Z||000006||80's BOY||05-13-2000||10:49 PM||||don't forget to change out the "o" rings top and bottom on your injectors,since you're already in there. about 10 bucks.||||reg||6
Z||000007||Oreif||05-13-2000||10:56 PM||||Since you are pulling it all apart why not find a set of 3.1L injectors? These are the "disc" type injectors and they don't carbon up like the stock Fiero injectors. I didn't notice any change in performance and maybe a 1/2 mile per gallon increase in gas mileage but they will retain there spray pattern better than the stock injectors.||||reg||1
Z||000008||GT Bastard||05-13-2000||11:44 PM||||great input guys... thanks||||reg||1
Z||000009||Carrolles||05-14-2000||11:23 AM||||I video taped the engine before I started my tear down and during the process.  It sure was handy to look back snd see how the wiring was actually routed especially where the flat wiring harness goes between the back side valve cover and the intake manifold and comes out under the alternator bracket by the thermostat.  Take your time and film every inch of the engine very slowly.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
